issue_context.body:
When enabling the new problem details service, the developer exception page middleware returns a JSON problem details to JSON-enabled clients but serializes the request path as an object instead of a string, likely due to the property on the payload inferring its type from `Request.Path` which is of type `PathString` (https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/main/src/Middleware/Diagnostics/src/DeveloperExceptionPage/DeveloperExceptionPageMiddlewareImpl.cs#L193)

<img width="222" alt="image" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/249088/189006149-f649bdb9-4bb1-4b36-8c97-8fbea98de355.png">

Following up reproduces this when it receives a request to `/throw`:

```csharp
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();

var app = builder.Build();

app.MapGet("/throw", () => throw new Exception("uh oh"));

app.Run();
```

